  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to exempting\nveterans and those on active duty from paying certain fees for travel",
    "basePrintNo": "S4441",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4441-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 40,
       "fullName": "Pete Harckham",
       "imgName": "1053_Pete_Harckham.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1233,
       "sessionMemberId": 2357,
       "sessionYear": 2025,
       "shortName": "HARCKHAM"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §9-0903, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4441REVISED 5/14/25\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nexempting veterans and those on active duty from paying certain fees for\ntravel\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo exempt veterans and active duty service members from fees collected\nfor travel on the New York world war veterans memorial highway in Essex\nCounty and the Prospect mountain veteran's memorial highway in Warren\nCounty.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Exempt veterans and active duty service members from fees\ncollected for travel on the New York world war veterans memorial highway\nin Essex County and the Prospect mountain veteran's memorial highway in\nWarren County.\n\nSection 2 - Provides effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe New York world war veterans memorial highway, which ascends White-\nface Mountain, and the Prospect mountain veteran's memorial highway,\nwhich climbs Prospect Mountain, honor the sacrifices and dedication of\nU.S. armed services members.\n\nAs such, those who served, or are serving, should be exempt from fees\ncollected to access the roadways. This is especially true ahead of the\n250th anniversary of the nation's founding on July 4, 2026.\n\nIn 2024, more than 7,500 veterans and active duty service members\naccessed the memorial highway on Whiteface Mountain, at a cost of $10\neach, according to the Olympic Regional Development Authority.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-2024: S7654 reported to Finance; A8181 referred to Environmental\nConservation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nApproximately $75,000 annually\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
